{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2SA",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass after this, that Absalom prepared him chariots and horses, and fifty men to run before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Absalom rose early, and stood beside the way of the gate: and it was ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that when any man that had a controversy came to the king for judgment, then Absalom called to him, and said, Of what city ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou? And he said, Thy servant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one of the tribes of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Absalom said to him, See, thy matters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good and right; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "deputed",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the king to hear thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Absalom said moreover, Oh that I were made judge in the land, that every man who hath any suit or cause might come to me, and I would do him justice!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that when any man came nigh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to do him obeisance, he put forth his hand, and took him, and kissed him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in this manner did Absalom to all Israel that came to the king for judgment: so Absalom stole the hearts of the men of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass after forty years, that Absalom said to the king, I pray thee, let me go and pay my vow, which I have vowed to the LORD, in Hebron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thy servant vowed a vow while I abode at Geshur in Syria, saying, If the LORD shall bring me again indeed to Jerusalem, then I will serve the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king said to him, Go in peace, So he arose, and went to Hebron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Absalom sent spies throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, As soon as ye hear the sound of the trumpet, then ye shall say, Absalom reigneth in Hebron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And with Absalom went two hundred men from Jerusalem, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " called; and they went in their simplicity, and they knew not any thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Absalom sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, David's counselor, from his city, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from Giloh, while he offered sacrifices. And the conspiracy was strong; for the people increased continually with Absalom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there came a messenger to David, saying, The hearts of the men of Israel are after Absalom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to all his servants that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him at Jerusalem, Arise, and let us flee; for we shall not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "else",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " escape from Absalom: make speed to depart, lest he should overtake us suddenly, and bring evil upon us, and smite the city with the edge of the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king's servants said to the king, Behold, thy servants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are ready to do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " whatever my lord the king shall appoint.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king went forth, and all his household after him. And the king left ten women ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " concubines to keep the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king went forth, and all the people after him, and tarried in a place that was far off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all his servants passed on by his side; and all the Cherethites, and all the Pelethites, and all the Gittites, six hundred men who came after him from Gath, passed on before the king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said the king to Ittai the Gittite, Why goest thou also with us? return to thy place, and abide with the king; for thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a stranger, and also an exile.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whereas thou camest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yesterday, should I this day make thee go up and down with us? seeing I go whither I may; return thou, and take back thy brethren: mercy and truth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Ittai answered the king, and said, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD liveth, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my lord the king liveth, surely in what place my lord the king shall be, whether in death or life, even there also will thy servant be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said to Ittai, Go and pass over. And Ittai the Gittite passed over, and all his men, and all the little ones that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all the country wept with a loud voice, and all the people passed over: the king also himself passed over the brook Kidron, and all the people passed over, towards the way of the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And lo, Zadok also, and all the Levites ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him bearing the ark of the covenant of God: and they set down the ark of God; and Abiathar went up, until all the people had done passing out of the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king said to Zadok, Carry back the ark of God into the city: if I shall find favor in the eyes of the LORD, he will bring me again, and show me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "both",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it, and his habitation:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if he shall thus say, I have no delight in thee; behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "here am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, let him do to me as seemeth good to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The king said also to Zadok the priest, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Art not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou a seer? return into the city in peace, and your two sons with you, Ahimaaz thy son, and Jonathan the son of Abiathar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "See, I will tarry in the plain of the wilderness, until word shall come from you to certify me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Zadok therefore and Abiathar carried the ark of God again to Jerusalem: and they tarried there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David went up by the ascent of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mount",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Olivet, and wept as he went, and had his head covered, and he went barefoot: and all the people that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him covered every man his head, and they went up, weeping as they went.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " told David, saying, Ahithophel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among the conspirators with Absalom. And David said, O LORD, I pray thee, turn the counsel of Ahithophel into foolishness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " David had come to the top ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the mount",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", where he worshiped God, behold, Hushai the Archite came to meet him with his coat rent, and earth upon his head;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom David said, If thou shalt pass on with me, then thou wilt be a burden to me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But if thou shalt return to the city, and say to Absalom, I will be thy servant, O king; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy father's servant hitherto, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I now also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy servant: then mayest thou for me defeat the counsel of Ahithophel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hast thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not there with thee Zadok and Abiathar the priests? therefore it shall be, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " whatever thing thou shalt hear out of the king's house, thou shalt tell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Zadok and Abiathar the priests.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " there with them their two sons, Ahimaaz Zadok's ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "son",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and Jonathan Abiathar's ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "son",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; and by them ye shall send to me every thing that ye can hear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.15.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.15.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Hushai David's friend came into the city, and Absalom came into Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
